    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d208-a1">

                <pb facs="0335" n="255" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg255"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fesler to Mr. Conger</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Consulate of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Amoy, China</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-06-14"><hi rendition="#italic">June 14,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 35.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your No. 1453, of the 13th
                    ultimo, regarding the granting to a Japanese of a monopoly of the camphor trade
                    in the Fukien Province, I have the honor to inclose herewith copies of the
                    regulations of the Fukien camphor board and the expert agreement recently signed
                    by the taotai and Japanese consul at Amoy.</p>
                <p>Since the agreement was signed the expert has returned to Japan presumably to
                    secure the amount of money he has to pay to the viceroy under the agreement. The
                    regulations, therefore, will not be enacted until his return.</p>
                <p>Taotai Yen, of Amoy, has been appointed controller of this newly established
                    board.</p>
                <p>Trusting that I shall have the benefit of your instructions in the premises, I
                    have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John H. Fesler</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Consul.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
